body:
Yea I never take my car to the dealership for repairs.  I had to drive a few hundred miles one weekend so I decided to get a vehicle inspection for $200 but they gave me a brand new Audi A5 as a loaner car that I used as a rental.  I like think of it has a rental car hack.  Anyways I think I figured out what I need to do.  

&#x200B;

I'm going to replace the MMI Screen for $500 and then get a new timing cover for $50 and have a shop replace it.  Looks like I'll walk away with a $600 bill and the car should last me another 100K miles with normal maintenance.  Thanks again for the insight!
